<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The V-Team brain's HTTP MCP server — the one process allowed to hold the
  PGLite lock.

  WHY THIS EXISTS AS A DAEMON. PGLite is single-writer. Before this, the lock
  was held by a `gbrain serve` that Claude Code spawned per session from a
  stdio MCP registration, which meant the holder was whichever session happened
  to start first, for as long as it happened to live. Every other resource then
  read nothing — silently, because the CLI printed the lock error and still
  exited 0. Three resources were degraded that way on 2026-08-16, one of them
  while ruling on a production PR.

  So the holder is now explicit, long-lived and owned by launchd rather than by
  a session: one server, loopback only, and every resource reaches the brain
  THROUGH it (MCP tools, or the CLI in thin-client mode). See docs/memory.md.

  RunAtLoad + KeepAlive, unlike beat/weekly which are deliberately neither: this
  is not a scheduled job that may be missed and caught up. It is the access path.
  If it is down, every resource falls back to reading the file directly, which
  is correct only while nothing holds the lock — so a server that dies and stays
  dead is exactly the ambiguity this whole change removes.

  --bind 127.0.0.1 is not a default worth losing: the tokens are long-lived
  bearer credentials with read access to every resource's memory.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>so.indianvcs.vteam.brain</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <!-- Through a login shell because gbrain is a bun-installed TypeScript
         entrypoint in ~/.bun/bin, which no launchd PATH contains by default.
         That missing directory is the same reason the old stdio registration
         reported ENOENT and never connected at all. -->
    <string>exec "$HOME/.bun/bin/gbrain" serve --http --port 7433 --bind 127.0.0.1 --token-ttl 31536000 --suppress-bootstrap-token</string>
  </array>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>GBRAIN_HOME</key>
    <string>__VT_BRAIN_HOME__</string>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>__VT_HOME__/.bun/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__VT_HOME__/.v-team/logs/serve-http.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__VT_HOME__/.v-team/logs/serve-http.log</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Restart if it exits for any reason. A dead holder is indistinguishable
       from a healthy one to a resource that only sees "no tools". -->
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Back off rather than spin: a brain that cannot open (corrupt lock, bad
       config) would otherwise be restarted continuously and fill the log. -->
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>10</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
